   "title": "README — H3 LongTake Render (motion + identity)",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 LongTake — Render (Ref2VA: motion + identity)\n\n**What it does.** A long video from a **source video**, clip by clip (124 frames = 5.2 s), with only one clip in VRAM/RAM. Each clip sees its own slice of the source as `<Video 1>` (motion, timing, camera) and the pictures as `<Picture 1..3>` (who is in it); the previous clip's last 5 latent frames are the anchor at frame 0. Clips are written to `output/h3_longtake/<project_name>/`: stop, resume (`mode=continue`), redo one clip (`redo_one`), assemble with the Stitch (audio from the source).\n\n**Setup.** `source_file` = a video in `input/` (ffmpeg decodes only the slice of each clip: any length, constant memory). `aspect=source`, 0.5 MP on 16 GB. Prompt: `<Video 1>` gives motion, timing and framing; `<Picture N>` the identity; say what to keep (\"keep the room… as in <Video 1>\") and what not to take from the picture.\n\n**Steps.** `dry_run=true` → the plan; `max_clips=2` → check the seam at 5 s; `max_clips=0` → everything; Ctrl+M on the Stitch.\n\nMeasured defaults: `context_frames=5` (clean seam and best adherence to <Video 1>), `anchor_mode=keyframe`, `seam_match=color`, 4 Turbo steps at 0.95."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## H3 LongTake — Render (Ref2VA: motion + identity)\n\n**What it does.** A long video from a **source video**, clip by clip (124 frames = 5.2 s), with only one clip in VRAM/RAM. Each clip sees its own slice of the source as `<Video 1>` (motion, timing, camera) and the pictures as `<Picture 1..3>` (who is in it); the previous clip's last 5 latent frames are the anchor at frame 0. Clips are written to `output/h3_longtake/<project_name>/`: stop, resume (`mode=continue`), redo one clip (`redo_one`), assemble with the Stitch (audio from the source).\n\n**Setup.** `source_file` = a video in `input/` (ffmpeg decodes only the slice of each clip: any length, constant memory). `aspect=source`, 0.5 MP on 16 GB. Prompt: `<Video 1>` gives motion, timing and framing; `<Picture N>` the identity; say what to keep (\"keep the room… as in <Video 1>\") and what not to take from the picture.\n\n**Steps.** `dry_run=true` → the plan; `max_clips=2` → check the seam at 5 s; `max_clips=0` → everything; Ctrl+M on the Stitch.\n\nMeasured defaults: `context_frames=5` (clean seam and best adherence to <Video 1>), `anchor_mode=keyframe`, `seam_match=color`, 4 Turbo steps at 0.95."
